  "body": "On the latest version of BitNet.cpp, a \"-cnv\" option was added.\nHowever, this option cannot work correctly.\n\nif you run \"run_inference.py\" with \"-cnv\" option is off, the following error is occured.\n\n```bash\npython run_inference.py --model /root/BitNet/models/Llama3-8B-1.58-100B-tokens/ggml-model-tl2.gguf --prompt 'AI is going to' --n-predict 128 --threads 32 --ctx-size 2048 --temperature 0.8\nerror: invalid argument:\nError occurred while running command: Command '['build/bin/llama-cli', '-m', '/root/BitNet/models/Llama3-8B-1.58-100B-tokens/ggml-model-tl2.gguf', '-n', '128', '-t', '32', '-p', 'AI is going to', '-ngl', '0', '-c', '2048', '--temp', '0.8', '-b', '1', '']' returned non-zero exit status 1.\n```\n\nI think the root cause of this issue is following line.\n\nhttps://github.com/microsoft/BitNet/blob/33ceabed0b421409c42106fb041af2151c83ea06/run_inference.py#L34\n\nI think we should implement like this...\n\n```python\n    command = [\n        f'{main_path}',\n        '-m', args.model,\n        '-n', str(args.n_predict),\n        '-t', str(args.threads),\n        '-p', args.prompt,\n        '-ngl', '0',\n        '-c', str(args.ctx_size),\n        '--temp', str(args.temperature),\n        \"-b\", \"1\",\n    ]\n    command.extend(\"-cnv\" if args.conversation else [])\n```",
  "closed_at": "2024-12-18T13:31:29Z",
